  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\n\nMulti-model consensus shows that upper level troughing will \nremain over Northern New England through at least early Monday\nbut will be losing its grip. This will mean mostly cloudy skies\nfor much of the area today with seasonably chilly temperatures.\nAs the trough begins to depart more sunny breaks are foreseen \nfor southern and far eastern zones later this afternoon. \nMostly dry weather is likely, other than a lingering chance for\nmountain snow showers.\n\nRidging then starts to move in to begin the work week, which \nwill lead to a gradual warming trend back to above normal \ntemperatures. On Monday, highs will mainly range from the upper \n30s to around 50 across the southeastern zones, but we will be \nback to widespread highs in the upper 40s to upper 50s by \nmidweek lower 60s likely at lower elevations. With high \npressure dominating, this coming week should remain dry. As of \nthis moment consensus shows a mainly dry and warmer than normal \nweekend is forthcoming.",
